# Synthetic carriers for the MP message ids no send site reaches (docs/findings/rl-mpmsg3.md §The last ids; src/rl_mpmsg3.c):
# the host side. mp-desync-p1 at f25050 = p1 (host, DAT_00553248 = 1) on the battlefield (DAT_0057c8fc = 2), 4 frames
# before the end (the actions builders file come due after it). A builder fills the send ring's slot 0 (0x512fb0: the
# ring wraps 39 → 1, slot 0 is never sent) through the write cursor DAT_00512f8c; its receiver then reads the same
# bytes back through the read cursor DAT_00515918 (a round trip). Scratch dwords: 0x512fb0 + 240.. (slot 0's tail).
scenario mp-desync-p1

# ---- the empty ones: 0 / 98 / 99, 31, 32, 78, 79, 81 (builder), 92; receiver 81 sets DAT_0058fe10 = 1
